    94	
    95	## Operator requirements
    96	
    97	Before enabling `go-repository-v1`, an operator supplies:
    98	
    99	- a fingerprinted Git release family covered by the rc.5 vectors;
   100	- HTTPS TLS and credential policy, or a trusted OpenSSH client, known-hosts
   101	  state, authentication state, and manager wrapper;
   102	- protected snapshot, receipt, artifact, journal, and marker storage;
   103	- resource limits at least as permissive as the shared-suite fixtures; and
   104	- an audit policy that treats the consuming skill and every effective external
   105	  repository as separate subjects.
   106	
   107	Every operation proves the full raw-object snapshot, scans every blob for the
   108	pinned Git LFS parser family, materializes and validates exact regular-file
   109	bytes, computes the build-source digest, and audits that frozen snapshot before
   110	artifact-cache lookup or compiler execution. This order also applies to a
   111	claimed cache hit and a source-covering dry run.
   112	
   113	Syntax-only offline validation may return
   114	`build_repository_unverified_offline` without claiming source coverage.
   115	Install, update, repair, and coverage-claiming audit fail
   116	`build_repository_source_unavailable` before mutation when exact source and
   117	audit evidence are unavailable. Read-only status does not contact the remote
   118	merely to re-test a tag.
